UID:5e5de8962468bfd2@nutcracker2026
DTSTAMP:20260914T010516Z
SEQUENCE:2026091401
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20261209T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20261209T205000
SUMMARY:Nutcracker: Cast A Dress Rehearsal – ACT II Cast A (Mandatory 
 – Production Week)
LOCATION:Robinson Center
DESCRIPTION:Wed. Dec. 9 · Call 7:30 PM · 8:10 PM–8:50 PM · Robinson 
 Center\nMANDATORY — production week. CALL TIME 7:30 PM: dancers must b
 e checked in and backstage by then\, so arrive by 7:15 PM. BA: Call Time
  is the time dancers should be check-in and backstage - Arrive 15 minute
 s before Call Time.\nACT II Dress Run\; In Performance Costumes\, Hair a
 nd Makeup.\nAll Casts are called unless a cast is named. SUBJECT TO CHAN
 GE — the BA master schedule\, the weekly BA emails and the BA portal a
 re the official source. Master: https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1
 xWFCPfY5m0aK9d5dnxvALNre-6-N7Cl0kkw24rvm6cE/\n\nCOSTUME / HAIR / MAKEUP 
 for Flowers: Flowers — Costume (you provide): Pink Seamless Tights\, P
 ink Bloomers\; Shoes: Pink Pointe Shoes w/ ribbons & elastics (clean\, q
 uiet\, unpancacked) *Dancers of Color may wear flesh-tone Pointe Shoes\;
  Makeup: Full Stage Makeup\; Hair: French Twist\; Accessories (BA provid
 es): Headpiece\nFull Stage Makeup Instruction Sheet:\n•  Apply foun
 dation and powder matching skintone\n•  Light skin tone eye shadow 
 over entire eye\n•  Dark brown eye shadow over crease\n•  Medi
 um brown eye shadow blended over brown\n•  Black fake eyelashes (no
 te: apply mascara to own lashes before application of fake lashes)\n• 
  Apply eyeliner after lashes dry\n•  Blush on the cheeks (be sur
 e to apply plenty so dancer doesn’t look washed out in the stage light
 s)\n•  Brown or tan on contour cheekbones\, hairline\n•  Use a
  brow pencil (or eyeshadow) to darken the eyebrows\n•  Red or Dark 
 Red Lipstick\nDancers of Color may wear flesh tone tights and flesh tone
  ballet shoes.\nCostume Care Guidelines:\n•  Handle costume pieces 
 with care while changing to prevent damage to delicate fabrics\n•  
 Promptly notify Ballet Arkansas in the event of costume damage at the po
 int of discovery\, no matter how significant\n•  Never throw costum
 es or accessories on the floor\, or hang costumes by their elastic strap
 s\n•  Refrain from sitting on the floor while in costume\n•  D
 o not attempt to alter\, mend\, clean\, or launder any costume or access
 ory\n•  Never apply stage make-up while in costume and shall take g
 reat care to refrain from smudging make-up on costume during its removal
 \n•  Refrain from the use of spray perfume or cologne while in cost
 ume\n•  Never wear any garment not assigned to cast member\n• 
  Do not handle or consume food or beverage while in costume\, with the e
 xception of water\n•  Do not remove costumes from their assigned dr
 essing rooms or from the theater\n•  Remove all bobby pins used to 
 secure head pieces and wigs following their use\n•  Return all head
 pieces to their assigned bags\n•  Comply fully with any and all upd
 ates to Ballet Arkansas’ wardrobe policies\n•  Do not pack marker
 s\, paints\, colored drinks or anything that may damage or stain costume
 s.
