SUMMARY:Nutcracker: Cast A Dress Rehearsal – ACT II Notes (Mandatory 
 – Production Week)
LOCATION:Robinson Center
DESCRIPTION:Wed. Dec. 9 · 9:00 PM–9:30 PM · Robinson Center\nMANDATOR
 Y — production week. BA: Call Time is the time dancers should be check
 -in and backstage - Arrive 15 minutes before Call Time.\nIn Performance 
 Costumes\, Hair and Makeup.\nAll Casts are called unless a cast is named
 . SUBJECT TO CHANGE — the BA master schedule\, the weekly BA emails an
 d the BA portal are the official source. Master: https://docs.google.com
 /spreadsheets/d/1xWFCPfY5m0aK9d5dnxvALNre-6-N7Cl0kkw24rvm6cE/\n\nCOSTUME
  / HAIR / MAKEUP for Flowers: Flowers — Costume (you provide): Pink Se
 amless Tights\, Pink Bloomers\; Shoes: Pink Pointe Shoes w/ ribbons & el
 astics (clean\, quiet\, unpancacked) *Dancers of Color may wear flesh-to
 ne Pointe Shoes\; Makeup: Full Stage Makeup\; Hair: French Twist\; Acces
 sories (BA provides): Headpiece\nFull Stage Makeup Instruction Sheet:\n
 •  Apply foundation and powder matching skintone\n•  Light ski
 n tone eye shadow over entire eye\n•  Dark brown eye shadow over cr
 ease\n•  Medium brown eye shadow blended over brown\n•  Black 
 fake eyelashes (note: apply mascara to own lashes before application of 
 fake lashes)\n•  Apply eyeliner after lashes dry\n•  Blush on 
 the cheeks (be sure to apply plenty so dancer doesn’t look washed out 
 in the stage lights)\n•  Brown or tan on contour cheekbones\, hairl
 ine\n•  Use a brow pencil (or eyeshadow) to darken the eyebrows\n
 •  Red or Dark Red Lipstick\nDancers of Color may wear flesh tone t
 ights and flesh tone ballet shoes.\nCostume Care Guidelines:\n•  Ha
 ndle costume pieces with care while changing to prevent damage to delica
 te fabrics\n•  Promptly notify Ballet Arkansas in the event of cost
 ume damage at the point of discovery\, no matter how significant\n• 
  Never throw costumes or accessories on the floor\, or hang costumes 
 by their elastic straps\n•  Refrain from sitting on the floor while
  in costume\n•  Do not attempt to alter\, mend\, clean\, or launder
  any costume or accessory\n•  Never apply stage make-up while in co
 stume and shall take great care to refrain from smudging make-up on cost
 ume during its removal\n•  Refrain from the use of spray perfume or
  cologne while in costume\n•  Never wear any garment not assigned t
 o cast member\n•  Do not handle or consume food or beverage while i
 n costume\, with the exception of water\n•  Do not remove costumes 
 from their assigned dressing rooms or from the theater\n•  Remove a
 ll bobby pins used to secure head pieces and wigs following their use\n
 •  Return all headpieces to their assigned bags\n•  Comply ful
 ly with any and all updates to Ballet Arkansas’ wardrobe policies\n•
   Do not pack markers\, paints\, colored drinks or anything that may 
 damage or stain costumes.
