 vent of costume damage at the point of discovery\, no matter how signifi
 cant\n•  Never throw costumes or accessories on the floor\, or hang
  costumes by their elastic straps\n•  Refrain from sitting on the f
 loor while in costume\n•  Do not attempt to alter\, mend\, clean\, 
 or launder any costume or accessory\n•  Never apply stage make-up w
 hile in costume and shall take great care to refrain from smudging make-
 up on costume during its removal\n•  Refrain from the use of spray 
 perfume or cologne while in costume\n•  Never wear any garment not 
 assigned to cast member\n•  Do not handle or consume food or bevera
 ge while in costume\, with the exception of water\n•  Do not remove
  costumes from their assigned dressing rooms or from the theater\n• 
  Remove all bobby pins used to secure head pieces and wigs following 
 their use\n•  Return all headpieces to their assigned bags\n• 
  Comply fully with any and all updates to Ballet Arkansas’ wardrobe po
 licies\n•  Do not pack markers\, paints\, colored drinks or anythin
 g that may damage or stain costumes.
